<%- include('partials/header') %><section class="page-hero compact"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-accent">FixMitra policy</span><h1><%= title %></h1><p>Plain-language information for using the FixMitra service platform.</p></div></section><section class="section"><article class="container legal-copy"><% if(kind==='privacy'){ %><h2>Information we collect</h2><p>FixMitra stores account details, service request information, addresses, quotations, status history and customer feedback only as needed to operate the platform.</p><h2>How information is used</h2><p>Data is used to review bookings, coordinate service professionals, prepare quotations, track status and provide customer support. Administrators receive only the information needed for these tasks.</p><h2>Account security</h2><p>Passwords are stored as secure hashes. Customer and administrator areas use separate role checks, and customers can access only bookings linked to their own account.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>Operational records are retained in the application database until an authorized administrator applies the business retention policy. Contact support for access or deletion requests.</p><h2>External services</h2><p>Email, WhatsApp, online payment and maps are not active unless valid credentials are explicitly configured. The application does not claim delivery or payment when integrations are unavailable.</p><% } else { %><h2>Service requests</h2><p>Submitting a booking creates a request with status “New.” It does not confirm technician availability, appointment timing or final price.</p><h2>Illustrative prices and quotations</h2><p>Displayed starting prices and demonstration quotations are estimates. Final scope and charges may vary after inspection. Quotations are not payment receipts.</p><h2>Customer responsibilities</h2><p>Customers must provide accurate contact, address and problem information and ensure safe access to the service area.</p><h2>Changes and cancellations</h2><p>Administrators may update or cancel bookings when service cannot be delivered. The complete change history remains visible in the tracking workflow.</p><h2>Platform availability</h2><p>FixMitra aims to keep the service available and secure but does not guarantee uninterrupted access during maintenance or third-party outages.</p><% } %><p class="legal-updated">Effective: 12 November 2026</p></article></section><%- include('partials/footer') %>